# Form validation (Zod)

Use **Zod** for all field and form validation in `component-lib-frontend/`. Do not add ad-hoc regex validators outside `src/validation/`.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/validation/schemas/fields.ts` | Reusable field schemas (`emailFieldSchema`, `passwordFieldSchema`, …) |
| `src/validation/schemas/forms.ts` | Full form objects + `z.infer` types |
| `src/validation/validate-field.ts` | `validateFieldValue()` → `{ valid, message }` |
| `src/validation/form-errors.ts` | `safeParseForm()`, `formatZodFormErrors()` |
| `src/validation/field-messages.ts` | `formFieldMessagesLive()` → FormField `error` / `success` |
| `src/types/fields.ts` | UI prop enums (`FieldSize`, `FieldStatus`, …) |
| `src/types/components.ts` | Page/template types + re-exported form value types |

Import: `import { … } from "@/validation"` or `@/types`.

## Field-level (live typing)

```tsx
import {
  emailFieldSchema,
  validateFieldValue,
  formFieldMessagesLive,
} from "@/validation";

const emailResult = validateFieldValue(emailFieldSchema, email, {
  successMessage: "Email looks good.",
});

<FormField
  label="Email"
  {...formFieldMessagesLive(emailResult, {
    touched: email.length > 0,
    submitted,
  })}
>
  <Input type="email" value={email} onChange={…} />
</FormField>
```

## Form-level (submit)

```tsx
import { registrationFormSchema, safeParseForm } from "@/validation";

const parsed = safeParseForm(registrationFormSchema, {
  firstName,
  lastName,
  email,
  password,
  terms,
});

if (!parsed.success) {
  setFieldErrors(parsed.fieldErrors);
  return;
}
// parsed.data is typed RegistrationFormValues
```

## Rules

1. **One schema per field** in `schemas/fields.ts` — reuse in form schemas via composition.
2. **Form types** = `z.infer<typeof myFormSchema>` in `schemas/forms.ts`; export via `src/types/components.ts` when used in pages.
3. Wire UI through **FormField** `error` / `success` / `warning` / `info` — not duplicate `<FieldError>` under the control unless standalone.
4. **Success messages** only after valid parse; use `formFieldMessagesLive` for touch/submit gating.
5. `@/utils/field-validation` is legacy — new code uses `@/validation` directly.

## New field checklist

- [ ] Add Zod schema in `schemas/fields.ts`
- [ ] Compose into form schema if needed
- [ ] Export inferred type if used outside validation
- [ ] Storybook/template demonstrates error + success states
